cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the EpiFlow Panel Builder, please cite it as below."
title: "Serrano Lab EpiFlow Panel Builder"
type: software
version: "1.4"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: BSD-2-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/SerranoLab/EpiFlow_Builder"
url: "https://serranolab.github.io/EpiFlow_Builder/"
abstract: >-
  A single-page web application for designing spectrally aware flow cytometry
  panels from the Serrano Lab reagent inventory, with dual-instrument detector
  mapping (Cytek Aurora 5L, BD FACSDiscover S8), conflict detection,
  alternative-conjugate suggestions, biotin/streptavidin pairing and a
  measured-spectra similarity matrix. Built around the EpiFlow histone
  post-translational-modification profiling platform.
authors:
  - family-names: Sreerama
    given-names: Sandeep
    affiliation: "Center for Regenerative Medicine, Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine"
  - family-names: Serrano
    given-names: Maria A.
    email: maserr@bu.edu
    affiliation: "Center for Regenerative Medicine, Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine"
keywords:
  - spectral flow cytometry
  - panel design
  - histone post-translational modifications
  - EpiFlow
  - antibody inventory
